{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550461-any-precedent-for-a-tamed-wight","id":1550461,"title":"Any precedent for a \"tamed\" Wight?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-28T13:16:04-07:00","id":1550461,"title":"Any precedent for a \"tamed\" Wight?","content":"I don't mean completely domesticated and I know they don't work with anybody outside of other wights in a pack but I'm running a new game and am thinking of the &quot;Mystery&quot; being a pack of wights roaming around that's managed to evade destruction and a thought crossed my mind. <br /> <br /> That thought was &quot;What if a Kindred was studying Wights and actively producing them to research the beast&quot; and instead of them escaping he actually let them go with a GPS tag but he only released the strongest willed ones that also were more likely to work together. They see the kindred more as another one of them and to some small degree acknowledge he was the one that helped them be rid of that pesky humanity that kept denying them their whims. As long as he feeds them, they'll not see him as prey and he can walk among them sort of thing?<br /> <br /> I know as the ST I can have whatever I want as the story but I try to at least have it not too far out of already established lore so yeah, anything like this ever happen in a book or ruleset of the past?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27150-minnzy","name":"Minnzy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T13:32:22-07:00","id":1550462,"title":"","content":"Nothing like this as far as I can remember.<br /> <br /> Wights aren't animals, they're not beasts, they're <b>The Beast<sup>TM</sup></b><sup>.</sup> I'm not even sure if one can be of significantly stronger will, they're all technically either pure will or devoid of will, depending on how you look at it. They're beyond the capacity of &quot;acknowledging&quot; anything.<br /> <br /> The mechanism through which Wights form bands is unknown, but it isn't conscious recognition. It's something mystical and reflexive, tied to the nature of the Beast.<br /> <br /> However you decide to conduct this scenario, you'll be basically determining things about one of the greatest mysteries of the setting, the truth behind the Beast. You can have a vampire that somehow gets treated as a member by this pack, but that's a monumental thing in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T22:51:45-07:00","id":1550473,"title":"","content":"They are their own Beast, basically<br /> BUT each Cainite's Beast is different and there are flaws and merits that let you &quot;customize&quot; your Beast to the point they become like the Shadow of a Wraith or the P'o of a Kuei-Jin<br /> Some Beasts are frighteningly intelligent even, but not necesarily wise or a &quot;human inteligence&quot; and even could be a Smeagol/Gollum situation<br /> Furthermore, depending of their inteligence, it is possible for a wight to retain some memories of his previous state of existence like abilities and retaining Linguistics rating only means that the wight can understand the languages it once knew (as opposed to actually speaking them)<br /> Also it is said, It has been observed that a vampire's Nature can influence its behavior as a wight and when not hungry they tend to pursue interests related to its former Nature. Only a wight whose Nature was that of a Monster will be... well... kill 0-24 monsters<br /> <br /> So in your scenario?<br /> With a tons of resource, a very lethal trial-and-error and basically &quot;sellective breeding&quot; (or pick the right specimen) having a pack of Wights, tagged with even a measure of influence on them (or more likely point them in the right direction then real influence/mastery over them - depend on the nature of the beast and the given Wight/Beast inteligence) is not out of the realm of possibility<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T18:19:44-07:00","id":1550496,"title":"","content":"With eastern vampires, there's an entire group of Devil Tigers that focus on controlling other vampires that have fallen to their Po/Beast. They control them and use them like hunting hounds. <br /> <br /> For kindred there's nothing official, but I could see it as some aspect of higher level Animalism. Animalism allows one to influence the Beast both in yourself and other vampires. So it's not hard to imagine some combination Animalism/Presence discipline sort-of allowing a kindred to influence wights, to some degree.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T17:54:49-07:00","id":1550614,"title":"","content":"Barring the use of that sort of power, I'd think that wights offer few advantages over just creating a pack of shovelheads as needed, and a lot more drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T14:42:13-07:00","id":1550671,"title":"","content":"A while back, I toyed with the idea of a Hellsing-style situation, where a vampire adopts a Path (I called it the Path of the Hound) that denies the Beast by subordinating the Kindred's will to a master of some kind (vampire or otherwise). Basically abdicating responsibility for their own morality, by leaving it to their master to maintain the reins of control.<br /> <br /> But obviously that's a character abandoning Humanity for a different Path, rather than OP's suggestion of a character commanding Wights that have fallen to the Beast completely. So, not really applicable.<br /> <br /> What I will say is that Disciplines could be employed to make a Wight act according to their master's will. At least as far as it goes. Presence could be used to ingratiate the Wight to the character (or intimidate them into compliance). Dominate just outright implants commands the Wight must obey. And, as stated before, Animalism deals directly with the Beast itself, cowing or subduing it. And a custom Animalism + Presence combo power could work to fill in some of the gaps.<br /> <br /> If the &quot;master&quot; has high enough Disciplines, they could potentially project commands from a distance, either through pure will or through voice (the latter being easier, if the Wight is rigged with an earpiece or collar that feeds orders to them). Combining GPS trackers with some kind of minder, like a non-Wight agent or an Animalism-controlled bird/rodent, to act as the master's eyes and ears for their Wight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:01:20-07:00","id":1550689,"title":"","content":"My take would be that this is something a number of vampires have tried over the centuries, but which always ends very, very badly because Wights aren\u2019t animals and cannot be tamed like animals: The Beast is too fundamentally diabolic an entity for one in it\u2019s thrall to reach any sort of equilibrium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}